cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "qkd-net-tools: QKD Network Analysis Toolkit"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-06-01"
abstract: >
  Python and R scripts for generating and validating large-scale QKD network
  topologies under realistic physical and technological constraints. Three case
  studies: Castile and León, Peninsular Spain, and the ADIF dark-fibre railway
  network. Includes topology generation (PAM k-medoids), structural analysis,
  BB84 secret-key-rate modelling, QKD-aware routing, and resilience simulations.
authors:
  - family-names: "García-Cobo"
    given-names: "Iván"
    affiliation: "Universidad de Salamanca"
    email: "ivangarciacobo@usal.es"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9472-5613"
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/ivgarci/qkd-net-tools"
keywords:
  - quantum key distribution
  - QKD
  - network analysis
  - complex networks
  - PAM clustering
  - BB84
  - resilience
  - dark fibre
  - ADIF

